  "title": "New Aveth President Elected",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "Having served as President of AVETH for one and a half years, Lars Büthe, a doctoral student from the Department of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering (D-ITET), has now stepped down from the post. The AVETH members thanked him for his efforts at the annual general assembly on the Hönggerberg campus on Tuesday evening, when they also elected his successor, Florian Thöle, a doctoral student from the Department of Materials (D-MATL). Thöle was already a member of the AVETH Board and leader of the association’s Politics Working Group (PoWoG).\n\nAlong with Florian Thöle, the following people have been elected to specific posts on the Board:\n\nThe following members have also been elected to the Board:\n\nFlorian Thöle. (Photo: Florian Thöle)\n\nThe AVETH members also noted the following milestones achieved during the past year:"
    }
  ],
